# Private dilemmas: only the owner of {A} sees the choice; the astronaut decides in
# character if nobody answers. Both options are decent; the cost is the point.
# The letter and dose dilemmas open personal threads (ow_letter, ow_dose).
# House style: content/STYLE.md.

# --- Thread: the dose ----------------------------------------------------------
card l_dose
type event
cat grim
due
once
days 9 9
roles A
when !is A ow_list
when !is A ow_song
when !is A ow_garden
when !is A ow_letter
when home A
text The weekly radiation summary puts {A}'s dosimeter at the top of the fleet's list, higher every week; the bunk sits on bare hull. The dose model issues {A} a "career remaining" figure. The form has a box for questions. It is very small.
do who ow_dose A
do open dil_dose

card dil_dose
type dilemma
once
cat grim
days 9 9
weight 1
duration 3
roles A
when !fired dil_dose
lean warm report keep
text Moving the bunk means telling the flight surgeon, who will want a meeting, and a meeting with the ground gets slower every week.
option report | Tell the surgeon | The meeting runs at more than a minute per question, and everyone learns to ask two at once. {A}'s bunk moves in beside the water tanks, and the reading drops by a fifth.
  set dose_told
  morale A -2
  trait A warm 2
option keep | Keep it quiet | {A} notes it privately and moves the sleeping bag to the other wall. It isn't nothing. It isn't a meeting either.
  set dose_hidden

card dose_swap
type beat
cat human
due
once
days 17 24
roles A B
when flag dose_hidden
when is A ow_dose
when cond B ok
text {B} reads the fleet's dose charts like the news, notices {A}'s numbers, and calls. {B}'s dosimeter has the newer calibration, and the two of them redo {A}'s week with it. That night {A} moves the bunk in beside the water tanks, and {B} stays on the line until it's done.
do bond A B 10
do bond B A 6

card dose_ok
type beat
cat human
due
once
days 17 24
roles A
when flag dose_told
when is A ow_dose
text The flight surgeon sends {A} a chart with one line on it, going down. Under it, by hand: "Thank you for telling me." "Fair," {A} writes back, and clips it beside the bunk.
do morale A 4

card c_dose
type beat
cat human
due
once
days 33 38
roles A
when is A ow_dose
when home A
text The entry mass budget wants the tank beside {A}'s bunk pumped down. {A} argues to keep it and runs the dose numbers to prove it. With this little cruise left, they don't. "Fine," {A} tells the ground. "Pump it." Then, because someone once checked on {A}: "Thanks for checking."
do trait A warm 1

# --- Thread: the letter ---------------------------------------------------------
card l_letter
type event
cat human
due
once
days 8 8
roles A
when !is A ow_list
when !is A ow_song
when !is A ow_garden
text The data drop brings {A} one file flagged personal, from the one person at home who never sends files.
do who ow_letter A
do open dil_letter

card dil_letter
type dilemma
once
cat human
days 8 8
weight 1
duration 3
roles A
when !fired dil_letter
lean warm now save
text The airlock is the one place aboard with no camera feed to the ground, so reading it now means reading it there. Saving it means carrying it unread until a quiet moment that may never come.
option now | Read it now | {A} reads it in the airlock and comes out ten minutes later without saying what it said. That evening {A} calls the other ships one by one, about nothing in particular.
  set letter_read
  morale A 6
option save | Save it | {A} saves it for a bad day. Every mission has one, and now {A} has something set aside for it.
  set letter_saved
  mark t_letter

card letter_open
type beat
cat human
due
once
days 26 34
roles A
when flag letter_saved
when is A ow_letter
when since t_letter >= 18
text It's a hard day, the kind {A} saved the letter for. {A} reads it in the airlock, once, and comes out with the last line by heart. {A} logs the airlock cycle and nothing else.
do morale A 12

card letter_worn
type beat
cat human
due
once
days 26 34
roles A
when flag letter_read
when is A ow_letter
text {A} has read the letter so often that the fold has worn through. {A} mends it along the crease and keeps it in the flight-suit pocket over the heart, which the checklist calls the "left chest pocket".
do morale A 4

card c_letter
type beat
cat human
due
once
days 34 35
roles A
when is A ow_letter
text In the restow for entry, item fourteen moves personal papers to the checklist binder. {A} reaches for the left chest pocket, where the letter has ridden since the data drop, finds it empty, and turns out the locker before the list explains it. "Item located," {A} logs.
do morale A 2

card a_letter
type beat
cat arrival
due
once
days 39 39
roles A
when is A ow_letter
text The entry checklist has a line for "personal items stowed". {A} reads the last line of the letter once more, aloud, then folds it into the left chest pocket, seals the flap, and ticks the box in ink.
do morale A 3

# --- Others ---------------------------------------------------------------------
card dil_gains
type dilemma
once
cat repair skill
days 5 32
weight 9
duration 3
roles A
when cond A ok
when home A
lean brave tune wait
text The attitude control on {A}'s ship has a slow wobble only {A} seems to notice. A switch to the alternate gain set would probably settle it. Procedure says the guidance team signs off any switch, and the console on shift wants the responsible engineer's signature.
option tune | Adjust it now | {A} selects the alternate set and watches the wobble die over six cycles. The ground signs off in the morning, after a non-conformance report and a long call, and adds a second signature line for next time.
  set gains_tuned
  who gains_who A
  trait A brave 2
option wait | Wait for sign-off | {A} files the request and lives with the wobble overnight. The ground approves {A}'s change, word for word, the next afternoon.
  trait A brave -2
  morale A 2

card gains_payoff
type event
cat repair skill
due
once
days 19 39
roles A
when flag gains_tuned
when flag trim_done
when is A gains_who
when cond A ok
when home A
text On the corridor burn, the attitude trace from {A}'s ship is a flat line, and every other ship shows the wobble {A} found. After the ground runs the fix through the simulator twice, {A}'s numbers go out to all seven, the report stapled to them.
do morale A 5
do res fuel 1

card dil_bracket
type dilemma
once
cat repair skill
days 8 36
weight 8
duration 3
roles A
when cond A ok
lean brave zip ticket
text {A} finds a hairline crack in a bracket holding a stowage rack, at a corner the model said would carry no stress. A proper fix means opening a ticket with Earth. A zip-tie fix takes five minutes.
option ticket | Open a ticket | Earth wants photos, measurements, and a part number that isn't on any drawing. {A} sends all three. The approved repair arrives a few days later and is, in every way that matters, a zip tie.
  morale A -1
option zip | Zip-tie it | {A} lashes the rack in a pattern no design review would pass, and it takes every load the ship can throw at it. The anomaly report calls it "interim". It is not interim.
  set zip_fix
  who zip_who A
  res spares -1
  morale A 3

card zip_back
type beat
cat repair
due
once
days 30 39
roles A
when flag zip_fix
when is A zip_who
when home A
text The stowage rack on {A}'s ship has carried its zip ties through every burn since. Before arrival {A} checks them all, adds one more for luck, and updates the anomaly report: "still interim".

card dil_eva_cam
type dilemma
once
cat repair
days 7 33
weight 7
duration 3
roles A
when cond A ok
when home A
when !is A eva_who
lean brave go wait
text An external camera on {A}'s ship has iced over, and its heater can't shift it. Clearing it now means the next ship closing up for an unscheduled window, someone suited on the other end. No one would blame {A} for waiting.
do who cam_who A
option go | Close up and go out | The ground's GO comes up on the next pass. With the next ship closed up and a suit at its hatch, {A} clears the lens in twenty minutes. On the way in, {A} photographs the fleet strung out against the dark. It becomes everyone's wallpaper.
  res fuel -1
  trait A brave 3
  morale A 4
option wait | Wait for the planned EVA | {A} waits. The camera stays blind for a few days, which the risk assessment calls acceptable. {A} has read all of it, appendix included.
  trait A brave -2

card dil_interlock
type dilemma
once
cat repair skill
days 10 36
weight 8
duration 3
roles A
when cond A ok
when home A
lean brave override vote
text The airlock on {A}'s ship won't cycle. One door sensor says "closed". The other says "ajar". The interlock won't move until they agree. The door is obviously closed, and {A} has the override code.
option override | Use the override | {A} reads the override to the next ship, hears it back, and starts the cycle; it stalls at ten kilopascals on a slow leak. Both sensors had a point: the door was closed, and a seal had crept a millimetre. {A} reseats it and opens a ticket.
  trait A brave 2
option vote | Find a third opinion | {A} pulls the lock's pressure trace as a tiebreaker. The door is sealed, and the "ajar" sensor is lying. {A} swaps it, the interlock is satisfied, and nothing was overridden.
  trait A curious 2
  res spares -1

